# Runtime source identity is measured byte-for-byte on every supported host.
# Never allow checkout configuration to rewrite reviewed loader sources.

# `deps.edn` is measured byte-for-byte too, and had no such protection.
# `kotoba.compiler.nbb.classpath/deps-digest` is sha256 over the FILE'S BYTES,
# and `deps-lock.edn` pins that digest -- so a checkout that rewrites the line
# endings makes the lock look stale on that host and only on that host. The
# failure names the one thing that did not happen (`deps.edn changed since the
# lock was generated`), and the fallback it triggers is `kbb -Spath`, i.e.
# the JDK-free property ADR-0202 exists to keep, lost on Windows.
#
# Observed 2026-09-01 on `browser-matrix (windows-2025)`: expected
# 4167621b..., actual 91188971..., and 91188971 is exactly sha256 of that same
# file with LF rewritten to CRLF. Earlier heads of the same branch passed on
# Windows with byte-identical content, so the conversion is a property of the
# runner rather than of the commit -- which is the argument for pinning it
# here instead of hoping.
deps.edn text eol=lf

# The adopted seed snapshot is digest-bound. Preserve its reviewed source bytes
# on Windows checkouts too; the native bootstrap is an opaque code payload.
seed/*.kotoba text eol=lf
seed/MANIFEST text eol=lf
seed/HEADS text eol=lf
seed/MEMORY-MAP text eol=lf
seed/SIR text eol=lf
seed/bootstrap/adopted-20261012.bin binary
seed/bootstrap/aarch64-linux-static-root.elf binary

# Diagnostic hashes bind raw native process bytes, including /proc whitespace.
# Do not normalize these records or "fix" launcher stdout to satisfy a linter.
docs/evidence/embench-native-diagnosis-20261026/** -text
docs/evidence/embench-native-diagnosis-20261026/**/*.stdout -whitespace
